1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,832
I get paid to erase people from existence. Every night, a black envelope gives me an address and three short hours.

2
00:00:09,132 --> 00:00:16,788
My task is simple: pack up their clothes, shred their letters, and wipe their hard drives clean like they never lived.

3
00:00:17,088 --> 00:00:26,544
The clients are people who want to disappear completely. No funeral, no tearful goodbyes, no trace left in the world.

4
00:00:26,844 --> 00:00:35,508
Tonight's address leads me to a small top-floor apartment. The door is unlocked, smelling faintly of old coffee and rain.

5
00:00:35,808 --> 00:00:43,488
I start boxing up silver framed photos on the desk. But when I look closely, my heart stops cold right there.

6
00:00:43,788 --> 00:00:51,924
The face smiling back in every picture is mine. My jacket, my scuffed boots, standing next to a laughing girl.

7
00:00:52,224 --> 00:01:00,840
I panic, dumping the closet onto the floor. My worn green bomber jacket is hanging there in three identical copies.

8
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:09,324
Under the mattress, I find a handwritten journal. The last entry reads: 'If you are reading this, the job worked.'

9
00:01:09,624 --> 00:01:18,072
I didn't take this job to erase strangers. I hired them to erase my own unbearable heartbreak after losing her.

10
00:01:18,372 --> 00:01:25,140
My hands tremble as I drop the final box into the incinerator. Would you delete yourself to stop the pain?
